#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114884 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ce098ff9-2ef1-5483-b057-b3fef12af16d" :question/math-academy-id "e-2477" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $\\mathbf f(t)+2\\mathbf g(t)$ with respect to $t$, where $$\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf f(t)&=(4t^2+9)\\mathbf i-\\frac1{t-2}\\mathbf j+\\cos(2t)\\mathbf k,\\\\\\mathbf g(t)&=(4t-1)\\mathbf i+e^{3t}\\mathbf j+\\cos(2t)\\mathbf k.\\end{aligned}$$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t))' = \\mathbf f'(t) + 2\\mathbf g'(t)\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivative of each function:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}{\\mathbf{f}}^{\\prime } ( t ) & = \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d} t} ( 4 {t}^{2} + 9 ) \\, \\mathbf{i} + \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d} t} ( - \\frac{1}{t - 2} ) \\, \\mathbf{j} + \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d} t} ( \\cos   2 t ) \\, \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = 8 t \\, \\mathbf{i} + \\frac{1}{( t - 2 {)}^{2}} \\, \\mathbf{j} - 2 \\sin   2 t \\, \\mathbf{k} , \\\\ {\\mathbf{g}}^{\\prime } ( t ) & = \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d} t} ( 4 t - 1 ) \\, \\mathbf{i} + \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d} t} ( {e}^{3 t} ) \\mathbf{j} + \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d} t} ( \\cos   2 t ) \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = 4 \\, \\mathbf{i} + 3 {e}^{3 t} \\, \\mathbf{j} - 2 \\sin   2 t \\, \\mathbf{k} .\\end{array}$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}( \\mathbf{f} ( t ) + 2 \\mathbf{g} ( t ) {)}^{\\prime } & = {\\mathbf{f}}^{\\prime } ( t ) + 2 {\\mathbf{g}}^{\\prime } ( t ) \\\\  & = ( 8 t \\, \\mathbf{i} + \\frac{1}{( t - 2 {)}^{2}} \\, \\mathbf{j} - 2 \\sin   2 t \\, \\mathbf{k} ) + 2 ( 4 \\, \\mathbf{i} + 3 {e}^{3 t} \\, \\mathbf{j} - 2 \\sin   2 t \\, \\mathbf{k} ) \\\\  & = 8 ( t + 1 ) \\, \\mathbf{i} + ( \\frac{1}{( t - 2 {)}^{2}} + 6 {e}^{3 t} ) \\, \\mathbf{j} - 6 \\sin   2 t \\, \\mathbf{k} .\\end{array}$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114885 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b19f5f01-948e-5f44-8016-63073ed31dbc" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Scalar Function Multiple Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3668609c-7f98-53ef-8aa7-6f9c3209dfee" :question/math-academy-id "e-2478" :question/problem "Find $(u(t)\\mathbf g(t))'$, where $\\mathbf g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\ln t\\\\-t\\\\e^{2t}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $u(t)=t$." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\big(u(t) \\mathbf g(t) \\big)' = u'(t) \\mathbf{g}(t) + u(t) \\mathbf{g}'(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find $\\mathbf g'(t)$ and $u'(t)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ng^{\\prime }(t) &= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{d}{dt}(\\ln t) \\\\ \\frac{d}{dt}(-t) \\\\ \\frac{d}{dt}e^{2t}\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2e^{2t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\nu^{\\prime }(t) &= \\frac{d}{dt}(t) = 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(u(t)g(t))^{\\prime } &= u^{\\prime }(t)g(t) + u(t)g^{\\prime }(t) \\\\\n&= 1 \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\ln t \\\\ -t \\\\ e^{2t}\\end{bmatrix} + t \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2e^{2t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}\\ln t \\\\ -t \\\\ e^{2t}\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -t \\\\ 2te^{2t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 + \\ln t \\\\ -2t \\\\ (2t + 1)e^{2t}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114886 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a146d5d3-2562-5b8b-886e-4cf6519d3282" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Chain Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cbb15346-028c-59c0-9b20-cd2f408c3bcb" :question/math-academy-id "e-2479" :question/problem "Find $(\\mathbf f \\circ u)'(t)$, if $\\mathbf f(u) = \\ln u \\, \\mathbf i + (u^2+5) \\, \\mathbf j + 4u \\, \\mathbf k$ and $u(t) =2t^3$." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "By the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf f \\circ u)'(t) = \\mathbf{f}'(u(t)) u'(t)\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivative of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{\\prime }(u) &= \\frac{d}{du}(\\ln u)i + \\frac{d}{du}(u^{2} + 5)j + \\frac{d}{du}(4u)k \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{u}i + 2uj + 4k, \\\\\nu^{\\prime }(t) &= \\frac{d}{dt}(2t^{3}) = 6t^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}( \\mathbf{f} \\circ  u {)}^{\\prime } ( t ) & = {\\mathbf{f}}^{\\prime } ( u ( t ) ) {u}^{\\prime } ( t ) \\\\  & = ( \\frac{1}{u ( t )} \\, \\mathbf{i} + 2 u ( t ) \\, \\mathbf{j} + 4 \\, \\mathbf{k} ) {u}^{\\prime } ( t ) \\\\  & = ( \\frac{1}{2 {t}^{3}} \\, \\mathbf{i} + 2 ( 2 {t}^{3} ) \\, \\mathbf{j} + 4 \\, \\mathbf{k} ) \\cdot  6 {t}^{2} \\\\  & = \\frac{3}{t} \\, \\mathbf{i} + 24 {t}^{5} \\, \\mathbf{j} + 24 {t}^{2} \\, \\mathbf{k} .\\end{array}$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114887 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54a6dbe-42cb-5614-ae0b-611de1719b45" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Product Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "228ae66f-9dad-5e6d-b405-9fbe62ecb7e9" :question/math-academy-id "e-2480" :question/problem "Find $\\dfrac{d}{dt}(\\mathbf f\\cdot\\mathbf g)(t)$, where $$\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf f(t)&=\\sqrt t\\,\\mathbf i+t^2\\mathbf j,\\\\\\mathbf g(t)&=\\frac1t\\mathbf i+e^t\\mathbf j.\\end{aligned}$$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Using the dot product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f} \\cdot \\mathbf{g})(t) = \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f}(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t) + \\mathbf{f}(t) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{g}(t))\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d} t} \\mathbf{f} ( t ) & = \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d} t} ( \\sqrt{t} ) \\mathbf{i} + \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d} t} ( {t}^{2} ) \\mathbf{j} \\\\  & = \\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{t}} \\, \\mathbf{i} + 2 t \\, \\mathbf{j} , \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d} t} \\mathbf{g} ( t ) & = \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d} t} ( \\frac{1}{t} ) \\mathbf{i} + \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d} t} ( {e}^{t} ) \\mathbf{j} \\\\  & = - \\frac{1}{{t}^{2}} \\, \\mathbf{i} + {e}^{t} \\, \\mathbf{j} .\\end{array}$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt} (\\mathbf f \\cdot \\mathbf g)(t) &= \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f}(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t) + \\mathbf{f}(t) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{g}(t)) \\\\[3pt] &= \\left(\\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}} \\,\\mathbf i +2t \\, \\mathbf j \\right) \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{1}{t} \\, \\mathbf i + e^t \\, \\mathbf j \\right) + \\left(\\sqrt{t} \\, \\mathbf i + t^2 \\, \\mathbf j \\right) \\cdot \\left(-\\dfrac{1}{t^2} \\, \\mathbf i + e^t \\, \\mathbf j \\right) \\\\[3pt] &=\\dfrac{1}{2t\\sqrt{t}} +2te^t + \\left(-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{t^2}\\right) + t^2e^t \\\\[3pt] &=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{2t^2} - \\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{t^2} +2te^t + t^2e^t \\\\[3pt] &= -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{2t^2} +\\left(2t+t^2\\right)e^t. \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115677 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54a6dbe-42cb-5614-ae0b-611de1719b45" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Product Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b029f1f-9e4a-597b-ae77-3d81c480f110" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60t^{3} + 15t^{2} + 14t + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113463} {:answer/id #uuid "cc3d915b-79a3-5034-a5de-c06db5adfc1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80t^{3} + 6t^{2} + 10t + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113464} {:answer/id #uuid "24835394-1f04-511b-a157-cfeb639fa83e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80t^{3} + 11t^{2} + 12t + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113465} {:answer/id #uuid "63aa8e90-8b39-5545-99b0-87f760920652" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60t^{3} + 7t^{2} + 10t + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113466} {:answer/id #uuid "7641f374-6267-5333-85c6-aaff569336a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80t^{3} + 15t^{2} + 10t + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7641f374-6267-5333-85c6-aaff569336a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80t^{3} + 15t^{2} + 10t + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113467} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f83259c-d6e0-5a5d-835f-1cdded5c1c51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113462}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a209f44d-4003-53ab-9d12-642d62514eb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-32298" :question/problem "Find $(\\mathbf f\\cdot\\mathbf g)'(t)$, where $$\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf f(t)&=20t\\mathbf i-2t\\mathbf j+(2+5t)\\mathbf k,\\\\\\mathbf g(t)&=t^3\\mathbf i+t\\mathbf j+(t^2+t)\\mathbf k.\\end{aligned}$$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "First form the dot product: $$\\mathbf f\\cdot\\mathbf g=20t^4-2t^2+(2+5t)(t^2+t)=20t^4+5t^3+5t^2+2t.$$ Differentiating gives $$(\\mathbf f\\cdot\\mathbf g)'=80t^3+15t^2+10t+2.$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115680 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a146d5d3-2562-5b8b-886e-4cf6519d3282" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Chain Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "949b7128-ac58-5a19-abd5-c446c6404838" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4t + 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113481} {:answer/id #uuid "a8e4e4cc-e41d-5275-8aba-ebb9127b417e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8t \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113482} {:answer/id #uuid "b3daaa61-1c5d-5b40-a9c2-237c16f4b80a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4t + 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113483} {:answer/id #uuid "c2e8a3fc-9fe9-55c1-9eed-507c1f94395c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8t + 8 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113484} {:answer/id #uuid "f3877b5f-6bb4-5d78-857c-eb8775ebe075" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2t \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2e8a3fc-9fe9-55c1-9eed-507c1f94395c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8t + 8 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113484} :answer-field/id #uuid "9cbc99ba-cc6c-5ec4-b8b5-c85bedb17f42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113480}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0fd1def5-bd75-572c-939f-770f964a1db9" :question/math-academy-id "q-32498" :question/problem "If \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{f} ( u ) = \\left[ \\begin{array}{c}2 u \\\\ {u}^{2} \\\\ 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n and $u(t) = 2t + 2$, then $( \\mathbf{f} \\circ  u {)}^{\\prime } ( t ) =$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "The chain rule gives $(\\mathbf f\\circ u)'=\\mathbf f'(u(t))u'(t)$. Since $\\mathbf f'(u)=\\langle2,2u,0\\rangle$ and $u'(t)=2$, $$(\\mathbf f\\circ u)'(t)=2\\langle2,2(2t+2),0\\rangle=\\langle4,8t+8,0\\rangle.$$"}]}
